 "nl": [
  "No packet from ntp-servers may enter guest-wifi, even for services open to everyone.",
  "Deny all traffic from nvr to printers (this overrides any public service).",
  "Hosts in mail may reach database over IMAP (TCP 143).",
  "Allow scada to connect to cameras using DNS over UDP 53 and HTTP (TCP 80).",
  "Deny all traffic from database to voip (this overrides any public service).",
  "Make DNS over UDP 53 on backup reachable from all internal zones.",
  "Allow backup to connect to nvr using IMAP (TCP 143).",
  "hr must accept SMB (TCP 445) and RTSP (TCP 554) and PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) from dmz-web.",
  "dns-servers is isolated: it may only reach backup on NTP (UDP 123); guest-wifi on DNS over UDP 53, and nothing else.",
  "Block SNMP (UDP 161) from cameras to guest-wifi; the rest of any UDP port between them is allowed.",
  "printers must accept MySQL (TCP 3306) and LDAP (TCP 389) from mail.",
  "dns-servers must never reach hr, regardless of any other rule.",
  "Block SMB (TCP 445), Telnet (TCP 23) from finance to backup; the rest of any TCP port between them is allowed.",
  "No packet from guest-wifi may enter printers, even for services open to everyone.",
  "hr must accept HTTPS (TCP 443) and IMAP (TCP 143) from backup.",
  "dev-lab is isolated: it may only reach ntp-servers on HTTPS (TCP 443), and nothing else.",
  "Block SNMP (UDP 161) from partners to mail; the rest of any UDP port between them is allowed.",
  "Allow dmz-web to connect to backup using SMB (TCP 445) and HTTPS (TCP 443) and NTP (UDP 123).",
  "printers offers HTTPS (TCP 443) to every zone.",
  "dev-lab must accept HTTP (TCP 80) and syslog (UDP 514) and RTSP (TCP 554) from backup.",
  "Allow voip to connect to printers using HTTP (TCP 80) and DNS over UDP 53.",
  "Hosts in printers may reach mail over DNS over UDP 53 and PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) and SMB (TCP 445).",
  "Deny all traffic from scada to voip (this overrides any public service).",
  "partners is isolated: it may only reach scada on DNS over UDP 53, and nothing else.",
  "Hosts in nvr may reach printers over DNS over UDP 53 and PostgreSQL (TCP 5432).",
  "Any zone may connect to voip over HTTPS (TCP 443).",
  "dmz-web must accept HTTPS (TCP 443) and SMB (TCP 445) from dev-lab.",
  "No packet from cameras may enter mail, even for services open to everyone.",
  "dns-servers offers HTTP (TCP 80) to every zone."
 ],
